# DeskCrab configuration
# Copy to ~/.config/deskcrab/deskcrab.conf and edit.

# Required: path to piper-tts voice model (.onnx)
PIPER_VOICE="$HOME/.local/share/piper/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx"

# Optional: piper length scale — controls speech speed.
# 1.0 = default. Lower = faster (e.g. 0.9 ≈ 10% faster). Higher = slower.
# PIPER_LENGTH_SCALE="0.9"

# Optional: piper speaker index — only used for multi-speaker models like libritts.
# Integer index (0-based) into the model's speaker map. Single-speaker models ignore this.
# PIPER_SPEAKER="79"

# Required: path to whisper.cpp model
WHISPER_MODEL="/usr/share/whisper.cpp-model-small.en/ggml-small.en.bin"

# Optional: Claude model and effort level
# CLAUDE_MODEL="opus"
# CLAUDE_EFFORT="low"

# Optional: project directory (Claude runs from here, gets project memory)
# PROJECT_DIR="$HOME"

# Optional: conversation archive directory
# ARCHIVE_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/deskcrab/archive"

# Optional: conversation timeout in seconds before archiving (default: 300 = 5 min)
# CONVO_TIMEOUT=300

# Optional: sliding-window history to keep long conversations cheap.
# Once the live convo exceeds CONVO_MAX_TURNS user/assistant pairs, the oldest
# CONVO_SUMMARIZE_TURNS pairs are folded into a running summary (kept above the
# recent turns) using CONVO_SUMMARY_MODEL. Recent turns stay verbatim.
# CONVO_MAX_TURNS=20
# CONVO_SUMMARIZE_TURNS=10
# CONVO_SUMMARY_MODEL="haiku"

# Optional: custom system prompt file — appended to the core prompt
# Use this for project-specific context, custom instructions, etc.
# CUSTOM_PROMPT="$HOME/.config/deskcrab/custom-prompt.md"

# Optional: whisper transcription fixes (sed expressions applied to transcribed text)
# Useful for proper nouns that whisper consistently gets wrong.
# Example: WHISPER_FIXES='s/mycool app/MyCoolApp/gi; s/\bhy plant\b/Hyprland/gi'
# WHISPER_FIXES=''

# Optional: TTS pronunciation fixes (sed expressions applied to spoken text)
# Useful for words piper mispronounces or spells out letter-by-letter.
# Applied only to the spoken reply — display-channel content is untouched.
# Example: TTS_FIXES='s/\bhmph\b/humph/gi'
# TTS_FIXES=''

# Optional: additional files to include in system prompt context
# Space-separated list of file paths. Their contents are appended to the prompt.
# CONTEXT_FILES="$HOME/project/CLAUDE.md $HOME/project/notes.md"

# Optional: durable "wants" file — the assistant's own long-term goals, which it
# maintains itself and pursues during autonomous wakes (crab wake / crab wake-at,
# or the systemd/deskcrab-wake.timer template). Unset = feature off.
# WANTS_FILE="$HOME/.local/share/deskcrab/wants.md"

# Optional: quiet hours (local time, HH-HH, wraps midnight) — autonomous wakes
# still run and can work silently, but never speak or open windows during these hours.
# WAKE_QUIET_HOURS="23-09"

# Optional: effort level for autonomous wakes (default: CLAUDE_EFFORT).
# Nobody is waiting on a wake, so it can afford more thinking.
# WAKE_EFFORT="medium"

# Optional: seconds without life signs before an autonomous wake is presumed
# hung and reaped (default: 300). There is no wall-clock limit on wakes — a
# session counts as alive while it streams output OR its process tree burns
# CPU (long compiles count as work). Raise it if your wakes run very slow,
# low-CPU tools in the foreground.
# WAKE_STALL_TIMEOUT=300

# Optional: detached background jobs — `crab job "<description>"` runs work as
# its own headless claude session under a transient systemd user unit
# (deskcrab-job-<id>), so it survives the turn that launched it and never
# holds the conversation open. Jobs are silent: no TTS, no windows; output
# goes to JOBS_DIR/<id>.log with a JSON status sidecar, listed by `crab jobs`.
# Jobs run unattended builds nobody is waiting on, so they default to the
# strongest model at high effort.
# JOBS_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/deskcrab/jobs"
# JOB_MODEL="fable"
# JOB_EFFORT="high"
# JOBS_SHOW_FINISHED=6     # finished jobs shown by `crab jobs` and in the prompt
# JOBS_KEEP_DAYS=14        # prune finished job records after this many days

# Optional: assistant persona name (default: Crab)
# The name the assistant sees in its system prompt: "You are <name>, a desktop
# voice assistant...". Set this to rename the assistant (e.g. "Beatrice",
# "Jarvis", etc). Also used as the notification/display title unless
# NOTIFY_NAME is set separately.
# ASSISTANT_NAME="Beatrice"

# Optional: assistant display name (default: ASSISTANT_NAME if set, else DeskCrab)
# Used as the notification title AND the title bar of the markdown display window.
# NOTIFY_NAME="DeskCrab"

# Optional: remote client (crab serve) — a phone talks to this machine.
# The assistant itself never moves: the phone is a microphone, a speaker, and a
# screen; the claude CLI, the prompt, the tools, and the conversation all stay
# here. Serving is off until SERVE_SECRET is set.
#
# Generate a secret with:  head -c 18 /dev/urandom | base64 | tr -d '/+='
# SERVE_SECRET="change-me"
#
# The listener binds loopback by default. Publishing it to a phone is a
# separate, deliberate act — a browser will not grant microphone access over
# plain HTTP, so put it behind TLS, e.g. Tailscale:
#   tailscale serve --bg https / http://127.0.0.1:8723
# SERVE_PORT=8723
# SERVE_BIND="127.0.0.1"
#
# Optional: seconds a single remote turn may take before it is abandoned.
# SERVE_TIMEOUT=600

# Optional: Web Push (crab notify) — reach the phone even with the page closed.
# Subscribe from the phone page's bell button; send with `crab notify <text>`.
# Needs the python-cryptography package (a stock system package on most
# distros); VAPID keys and subscriptions live under
# ~/.local/share/deskcrab/webpush/. PUSH_SUBJECT is the RFC 8292 `sub` claim —
# how the push service's operators could reach the sender (mailto: or https:
# URL). The default identifies this project on GitHub.
# PUSH_SUBJECT="mailto:you@example.com"
